   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of new programmes, policies and initiatives developed thanks to the programme, that foster more inclusive markets for livelihood and employment</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2015">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">0</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">PFP organized to bring together key stakeholders for each short-listed proposal 
Contract 3 catalytic grantees and disburse first tranches of each of the USD200,000 grant

The food value chain greening manual finalization and conducting food value chain greening training sessions</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1 Food value chain greening manual published
4 Online regional training sessions conducted 
2 Catalytic grantees contracted in east Africa (Kilimo Trust) and Southern Africa (AFAP)
2 PFPs conducted with Kilimo Trust (Tanzania) and AFAP (Malawi) and respective stakeholders
1 online food value chain greening course being tested</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">launch the online food value chain greening course
Develop 3 knowledge products relating to the 3 food value chain greening projects being undertaken in Tanzania &amp; Uganda; Malawi and Burkina Faso by Kilimo Trust, AFAP and INERA respectively
West African catalytic grantee contracting</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">5 Country Specific Value chain greening training sessions conducted
1 online food value chain greening course being launched and trained over 400 participants
West African catalytic grantee INERA contracted
3 Knowledge product development consultants recruited. Inception report and workplan developed successfully</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhanced regional &amp; national actors capacity to develop sustainable and resilient value chains</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Resilient Food System (GEF IAP) Country office, AGRA and UNDP country offices contact established in line with value chain greening manual training needs establishment.

Part of these activities deferred to next year due to the covid 19 pandemic outbreak, these included the finalization of the development of the food value chain greening manual as well as the conducting food value chain greening training sessions</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
